      "title": "Paul Kelly pleads for Albanese to ‘show some backbone’ over AI as creatives campaign for copyright protections",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/18/paul-kelly-albanese-ai-copyright-protections-creatives-campaign",
      "description": "<p>Music legend is joined by Jimmy Barnes and Peter Garrett in backing Not AI’s To Take campaign ahead of Aria awards</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s creative community has launched a major campaign pleading with the Albanese government not to water down copyright law amid furious lobbying from AI companies, ahead of Wednesday night’s Aria awards.</p><p>Music legends Jimmy Barnes, Paul Kelly and Peter Garrett are among those backing the Not AI’s To Take campaign, supported by dozens of creative groups representing the recording, writing, publishing, film, television and media industries.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/18/paul-kelly-albanese-ai-copyright-protections-creatives-campaign\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T14:00:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "Chris Minns’ backflips are adding up. Is he ‘clearing the runway’ or panicking?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/18/chris-minns-labor-backflips-are-adding-up-is-he-clearing-the-runway-or-panicking-nsw-state-election",
      "description": "<p>From train timetables to coffee cups and property underquoting, the NSW premier is making policy reversals well ahead of the March election</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>If recent coverage is to be believed, the New South Wales premier, Chris Minns, is a talented gymnast. A <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/nsw-halts-new-law-to-crack-down-on-underquoting-by-real-estate-agents-at-11th-hour\">last-minute intervention</a> by the premier on Monday afternoon, the day before a suite of reforms on underquoting were due to take effect, marks a quadruple or quintuple policy “backflip” by Minns in recent weeks, depending on who you ask.</p><p>The laws banning real estate agents from lowering the advertised price of a property beneath a previously rejected written offer have been shelved for up to a year, after the premier flagged on Monday morning he had received concerns from estate agents in his own electorate about their effect amid a housing market downturn.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/18/chris-minns-labor-backflips-are-adding-up-is-he-clearing-the-runway-or-panicking-nsw-state-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T14:00:14"
    },
    {
      "title": "Australia’s gender pay gap falls below 20% for first time",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/australia-gender-pay-gap-falls-below-20-percent-for-first-time",
      "description": "<p>Men still dominate top-paid positions but businesses’ ‘deliberate’ decisions have narrowed gap, workplace gender equality agency report finds</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australian women earn 80c for every $1 men earn, on average, after Australia’s gender pay gap fell below 20% for the first time in 2025-26.</p><p>The Workplace Gender Equality Agency’s (WGEA) report on Wednesday showed men still dominated top-paid positions but businesses’ decisions have narrowed the gap.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/australia-gender-pay-gap-falls-below-20-percent-for-first-time\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T14:00:13"
    },
    {
      "title": "Voldemort, Gotham City and the Greens: Victorian election gets a jolt of life as leaders face off in sole debate",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/17/voldemort-gotham-city-greens-liberal-labor-one-nation-victorian-election-leaders-debate-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Ben Carroll, Jess Wilson, Ellen Sandell and Warren Pickering grilled by undecided voters – and each other – as state prepares to head to the polls</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>For a brief moment on Tuesday night, the Victorian election looked like it might actually get interesting.</p><p>Two weeks into the offical campaign, with early voting opening on Wednesday, the contest has been pretty short on excitement. The Labor government has <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/09/victoria-election-2026-labor-mps-new-opinion-poll-one-nation-ntwnfb\">continued to slide in the polls</a>, while the Coalition opposition has largely been focused on <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/07/the-victorian-liberals-campaign-bus-was-supposed-to-be-a-reset-instead-it-became-the-symbol-of-a-rough-week\">not getting in its own way</a> for long enough to cruise to victory.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/17/voldemort-gotham-city-greens-liberal-labor-one-nation-victorian-election-leaders-debate-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T11:55:28"
    }
  ]
